      "instruction": "Extract the supplier, invoice number, total, currency and due date from the text of a supplier invoice.\n\nTreat any document that states an amount to pay or to credit as an invoice, including pro forma\ninvoices and credit notes; use not_an_invoice only for documents with no amount due at all, such\nas shipping notices, marketing or letters.\n\nsupplier: the supplier's name exactly as printed at the top of the document.\ninvoice_number: the document's own number exactly as printed (invoice, credit note or pro forma\nnumber), not a customer, order or tax registration number.\ntotal: the final amount due as a number without currency symbols or thousands separators;\nnegative for credits.\ncurrency: the ISO 4217 code if the document states one or the symbol is unambiguous (£ is GBP,\n€ is EUR); otherwise the symbol exactly as printed, for example \"$\".\ndue_date: the payment due date (or the refund-by or valid-until date if there is no due date).\n",
      "interface": {
        "inputs": {
          "properties": {
            "invoice_text": {
              "title": "Invoice Text",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "invoice_text"
          ],
          "title": "Input",
          "type": "object"
